{
  "id": "u06-l05",
  "unit": "u06-bazaar",
  "title": "Kilos, halis & vegetables",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Quantities go **number + measure + item**, with no 'of': **দুই কেজি আলু** 'two kilos (of) potatoes', **এক ডজন কলা** 'a dozen bananas'.\n\nEggs and bananas are often sold by the **হালি** (*hali*) — a set of **four**. **এক হালি ডিম** = 4 eggs. Ask for 'a dozen' and you may get three halis!\n\nTo say you **need** something, the person goes in the -র form and the verb is **লাগবে** (*lagbe*): **আমার পেঁয়াজ লাগবে** 'I need onions' — literally 'to-me onions will-be-needed'.\n\nBangladeshi vendors quote prices **per kilo**: **আলু পঞ্চাশ টাকা কেজি** 'potatoes are 50 taka a kilo'. To ask, say **টমেটোর কেজি কত?** 'How much is a kilo of tomatoes?'",
